        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Dy(CF3SO3)3·6H2O (0.3 mmol) was added to a solution of H2L1 (0.2 mmol) in 16 mL of methanol/dichloromethane (1:1, v/v), then NaN3 (0.4 mmol) was added. The solution was stirred for 3 h, filtered, and the filtrate was left undisturbed for slow evaporation. Yellow crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were collected after 5 days. Caution: NaN3 is potentially explosive and should be used carefully in small amounts.",
